Orders of 40 or more get 10% off. To apply the discount to a total, take 10%
off when the total is at least 40.
    1. Define a function apply_discount that takes a decimal number total and
       gives back a decimal number.
    2. In apply_discount: if total is at least 40, give back total times 0.9.
    3. In apply_discount: otherwise give back total unchanged.
    Assumption: 10% off means multiplying by 0.9.
    Compiler: `apply_discount` takes `total` as a decimal number, from how it is
        used.
    Compiler: `apply_discount` gives back a decimal number, from what it
        returns.
